## Backend/Admin SDK (Server-Side Only)

### Firebase Admin SDK Credentials

**Do NOT commit service account keys to version control.**

1. Firebase Console → Project Settings → Service Accounts
2. Click "Generate New Private Key"
3. Save the JSON file locally, add to `.gitignore`
4. For Vercel: Set as environment variable (not recommended) or use Firebase Admin SDK with environment variables

### Option A: Service Account Key File (.env.local)

```env
# Path to Firebase Admin SDK service account key (local development only)
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH=./service-account-key.json
```

Store the key in root directory (add to `.gitignore`):
```
service-account-key.json
```

Content format:
```json
{
  "type": "service_account",
  "project_id": "futurecapsule-dev",
  "private_key_id": "...",
  "private_key": "-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n",
  "client_email": "firebase-adminsdk-abc@futurecapsule-dev.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
  "client_id": "...",
  "auth_uri": "https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth",
  "token_uri": "https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token",
  "auth_provider_x509_cert_url": "https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs",
  "client_x509_cert_url": "..."
}
```

### Option B: Environment Variables (For Vercel/CI)

Convert the JSON key to a base64-encoded string:
```bash
cat service-account-key.json | base64 | tr -d '\n'
```

Set as environment variable:
```env
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64=ewogICJ0eXBlIjog...
```

In code:
```typescript
const serviceAccountKey = JSON.parse(
  Buffer.from(process.env.FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64!, 'base64').toString('utf-8')
);
```

